5. STATUTORY INTEROPERABILITY & CLEANROOM SPECIFICATION NOTICE
================================================================================

Pryzma is an independent compatibility engine designed to restore visual resource pack
and shaderpack functionality in modern Minecraft runtimes.

All format parsers, runtime adapters, and specification handlers for legacy resource pack
features (including `.properties` files, CTM tile connection rules, CIT item matchers,
and CEM skeletal models historically popularized by OptiFine and MCPatcher) are independent
cleanroom implementations developed solely for technical interoperability. Pryzma contains
no proprietary source code or binaries from OptiFine or MCPatcher.

Interoperability and technical adaptation are established and protected under:
- United States Copyright Act (17 U.S.C. § 107 - Fair Use for Interoperability;
  Sega Enterprises Ltd. v. Accolade, Inc., 977 F.2d 1510; Sony Computer Entertainment,
  Inc. v. Connectix Corp., 203 F.3d 596; Google LLC v. Oracle America, Inc., 141 S. Ct. 1162);
- European Union Directive 2009/24/EC, Article 6 (Decompilation & Interoperability);
- Civil Code of the Russian Federation, Part IV, Article 1280 (Right of Legitimate
  Users to Decompile and Adapt Software for Technical Interoperability).

Pryzma is not affiliated with, sponsored by, or endorsed by Mojang Studios,
Microsoft Corporation, or predecessor closed-source modification authors.
Minecraft is a trademark of Mojang AB. OptiFine is a trademark/project of sp614x.
All trademarks are used exclusively in a nominative capacity to declare format compatibility.
